# TypeScript

Strict mode stays on. Parse untrusted JSON with Zod and infer the type from the schema.

```ts
export const movieSchema = z.object({
  id: z.number(),
  title: z.string(),
  posterPath: z.string().default(''),
});

export type Movie = z.infer<typeof movieSchema>;
```

## Rules

- `async`/`await` only. No floating promises.
- List endpoints drop a bad item. Detail endpoints fail the query if the object is invalid.
- Empty poster or backdrop paths become `""`, not a broken image URL.
- Public functions get a one-line comment when the name is not enough. Do not narrate obvious lines.

## Do not

- Duplicate a Zod type as a hand-written interface
- Catch an error and return an empty list for a detail request
- Use `as Movie` on raw JSON
